1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,048
Narrator: Scenario 93. Follow up and operational improvement.

2
00:00:06,648 --> 00:00:16,320
B: We've agreed to improve alerting and update the recovery runbook. Can I record one action saying the operations team will handle both items?

3
00:00:16,920 --> 00:00:26,880
A: Let's split them into separate actions with one accountable owner each. Otherwise, a partial update could make the whole improvement appear complete.

4
00:00:27,480 --> 00:00:38,400
C: I'll own the alerting action. The current rule reacts only when the queue is already full, so I propose detecting sustained processing delays earlier.

5
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:50,472
A: What proves completion? We should specify the failure to replay, the maximum detection time, and how we confirm the notification reaches the correct on-call engineer.

6
00:00:51,072 --> 00:01:01,872
C: In the test, we'll stop a worker and replay representative traffic. The alert must fire within two minutes and reach the assigned on-call route.

7
00:01:02,472 --> 00:01:14,208
B: That covers detection, but could the rule also page constantly during normal low traffic? Please include evidence that it handles expected quiet periods appropriately.

8
00:01:14,808 --> 00:01:26,952
C: Agreed. I'll test the quiet-period behavior and attach both results. I can commit to a reviewed rule by November 18 at 12:00 UTC.

9
00:01:27,552 --> 00:01:38,736
A: I'll own the runbook action separately. Acceptance will require another engineer to follow the steps, identify the stop condition, and complete the recovery check.

10
00:01:39,336 --> 00:01:49,536
B: Who will review that exercise, and does your due date depend on the alerting change being finished first? We should show any sequencing explicitly.

11
00:01:50,136 --> 00:02:00,672
A: The service lead will review it. The recovery steps can be validated independently, but I'll link the final alert reference after the monitoring review.

12
00:02:01,272 --> 00:02:11,856
C: I will share the proposed alert details early so the runbook doesn't wait unnecessarily. Any change to our commitment will be recorded with the reason.

13
00:02:12,456 --> 00:02:24,744
B: I'll create two tracked actions with those owners, criteria, and dependencies. We'll check progress on November 16 and keep completion evidence attached to each record.
